    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A port on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elbe">Elbe</a> that grew from the Carolingian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hammaburg">Hammaburg</a> and a twelfth-century merchant town into the Hanse's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-sea">North Sea</a> gateway.</li><li>Neutral behind its walls in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-tyrants">the Thirty</a> Years' War, it became the largest and richest city of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> and a centre of music and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theatre">theatre</a>.</li><li>Annexed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> and wrecked in 1943, it survives as a city-state of the Federal Republic and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>'s largest port.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hamburg">Hamburg</a> celebrates its port's birthday every May on the strength of a charter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-barbarossa">Frederick Barbarossa</a> dated 1189 that historians have shown to be a thirteenth-century forgery.</p></aside>
    </section>

